  "issues": [
    {
      "id": "18206",
      "key": "SFCC-123",
      "summary": "Spike: Contentful Integration Technical Design & Content Model",
      "description": "Objective\nUnderstand the Contentful integration architecture, define the content models required for SFCC, and identify what the Accenture squad needs to build on the SFCC side before the dedicated Contentful squad comes onboard.\nBackground\nContentful is the CMS for Zimmermann's storefront content (page layouts, editorial, imagery, assets, navigation, and merchandising). A separate Contentful SOW and squad are incoming — they will own the full Contentful setup. However, there is significant SFCC-side work required to integrate with Contentful via MRT, and the team needs an early understanding of the content model structure and integration pattern before that squad arrives.\nTim has confirmed the team needs to set up layouts and content models, and understand the integration deeply enough to build the SFCC-side connection correctly.\nTasks\nDocument the Contentful → MRT → SFCC integration pattern and data flow\nIdentify which content types are required in Contentful for Sprint 1 and 2 (e.g. page layouts, content slots, editorial components)\nDefine what the SFCC side needs to consume from Contentful: which APIs, which content model fields, what rendering logic\nIdentify locale configuration requirements in Contentful aligned to the 8 storefronts\nClarify the handoff boundary: what Accenture builds vs what the incoming Contentful squad owns\nFlag any blockers or dependencies that need to be resolved before the Contentful squad onboards\nDefinition of Done\nA technical design document is produced covering the Contentful integration architecture, content model requirements, locale setup, and SFCC-side build scope — ready to be shared with the incoming Contentful squad as a briefing artefact.",
      "status": {
        "name": "Done",
        "category": "Done",
        "color": "green"
      },
      "assignee": {
        "display_name": "Jhoan Rose Dela Cruz",
        "name": "Jhoan Rose Dela Cruz",
        "email": "jhoan.rose.dela.cruz@accenture.com",
        "avatar_url": "https://avatar-management--avatars.us-west-2.prod.public.atl-paas.net/712020:26b54c48-03dc-4b75-9a3b-4e924b0a4580/f69f9733-9221-48a9-aada-84ece49d3074/48"
      },
      "updated": "2026-08-10T12:57:09.278+1000"
    },
    {
      "id": "18205",
      "key": "SFCC-122",
      "summary": "Spike: Document SFCC MRT API Capabilities",
      "description": "Objective\nDocument the available SFCC MRT (Managed Runtime) APIs relevant to the Zimmermann storefront build, so the squad has a clear picture of what is available for product, pricing, and category data consumption before MuleSoft is ready.\nBackground\nMani has identified that the base BM configuration is in place but product and price data are currently missing as MuleSoft is not yet ready. Understanding the MRT API capabilities will help the squad determine what can be built and tested in lower environments in the meantime.\nAngelo to set up session with Mani/Victor\nTasks\nReview and document available MRT APIs relevant to SFCC: endpoint structure, payload format, authentication, and data available\nAssess which MRT APIs can serve product, category, and pricing data in lower environments while MuleSoft is not yet available\nIdentify any limitations or gaps that will need to be covered by MuleSoft once it is ready\nConfirm which MRT APIs are permanent parts of the architecture vs workarounds for the current state\nDefinition of Done\nA documented inventory of relevant MRT APIs is produced and shared with the squad, sufficient to unblock BM configuration and front-end development in lower environments.",
      "status": {
        "name": "Done",
        "category": "Done",
        "color": "green"
      },
      "assignee": {
        "display_name": "Marcel Angelo Navarro",
        "name": "Marcel Angelo Navarro",
        "email": "marcel.a.n.navarro@accenture.com",
        "avatar_url": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/482e2e100517026f4980d6455214aa11?d=https%3A%2F%2Favatar-management--avatars.us-west-2.prod.public.atl-paas.net%2Finitials%2FMN-6.png"
      },
      "updated": "2026-08-10T12:57:10.783+1000"
    },
    {
      "id": "17827",
      "key": "SFCC-1",
      "summary": "Platform Setup & Environments",
      "description": "Epic Summary\nProvision and configure all SFCC Business Manager environments (dev, staging, prod) and establish the foundational platform settings required before any build work can begin. This epic unblocks all other epics across both squads.\nBusiness Value / Objective\nWithout environments stood up and correctly configured, no build or testing can happen. This is the critical path item for sprint 1 — getting SFCC and MRT environments live, with correct site IDs, permissions, and storefront config across all 8 storefronts, is the prerequisite for every other epic on the board.\nScope\nIn Scope:\nProvision SFCC Business Manager instances for dev, staging, and production\nConfigure site IDs, locales, currencies, and tax jurisdictions for all 8 storefronts\nSet OCAPI/SCAPI permissions for PWA Kit API access\nPWA Kit scaffold and MRT config, local dev environment setup\nCI/CD pipeline including lint, unit tests, bundle size gate, Playwright P0 suite, and Lighthouse CI >90\nRegional feature flags to support canary go-live strategy\nOut of Scope:\nStorefront-level business configuration (languages, translations, tax rules) — covered in Regional Storefronts (SFCC-19)\nDesign system / UI library component setup — covered in PWA Kit Components (SFCC-2)\nAny functional build work (cart, checkout, PDP, etc.)\nDependencies\nZimmermann to provide access to SFCC licences, Business Manager, GitHub, and CI/CD tooling\nMuleSoft API contracts confirmed before build commences\nSalesforce MRT environment provisioning\nAssumptions & Constraints\n8 storefronts in scope: AU, US Domestic, US International, UK, EU Domestic, EU International, HK, ME",
      "status": {
        "name": "In Progress",
        "category": "In Progress",
        "color": "yellow"
      },
      "assignee": {
        "display_name": "Manikandan Ramachandran",
        "name": "Manikandan Ramachandran",
        "email": "m.m.ramachandran@accenture.com",
        "avatar_url": "https://avatar-management--avatars.us-west-2.prod.public.atl-paas.net/557058:a8d3e24a-618f-49c2-a524-9f82f1ad6b1b/966dfce7-a58a-45eb-bdcc-09adceb8e773/48"
      },
      "updated": "2026-08-10T12:57:19.023+1000"
    }
  ]
}"}

